## Branch

- `phase/N-short-slug`, `epic/P?-E?-short`, or `feat/…` for a **coherent code cluster**.
- Do **not** open a separate PR for every micro-task, handoff, or PM docs pass.

## Commits

- Commit when a **coherent unit** is ready (prefer batching related Task IDs) — **OK during freeze** (local / feature branch).
- Handoff files are **required on disk** for the role pipeline — they do **not** require their own commit or PR.
- Leave the tree dirty across Dev→QA→PM on the same cluster until the unit is ready to commit.
- Still commit before any future push/PR (no huge unreviewed dump).

## When to open a PR (after 2026-09-01 only)

Open **push + `gh pr create --base main`** only when **all** of these hold:

0. **Today’s date is on or after 2026-09-01** (or user explicitly ended the PR freeze), **and**
1. There is **substantive code** (crates / apps) in the branch vs `main`, **and**
2. Either the **code cluster is Done** (QA Pass + enough to ship), **or** the user explicitly says «PR» / «открой PR» / «закрой epic», **and**
3. There is **no open PR** already for this head branch.

**Do not open a PR for:**
- anything before the freeze ends (unless user lifts it)
- handoffs only (`docs/handoffs/*`)
- roadmap / canvas / status docs only
- a second PR that duplicates an existing open/merged PR on the same branch tip
- stale `SPRINT-GATE` / `PR-GATE` markers that are already MERGED/ARCHIVED

**Docs separately:** PM can update `SPRINT_ROADMAP.md`, `12-development.md`, catalog notes, canvas **without** a dedicated PR — fold into the next code PR after the freeze, or a small docs commit later when the user asks. Handoffs may land with that same docs/code commit.

## Roles (git only)

| Role | Git expectation |
| :--- | :--- |
| Dev/UX | Handoff on disk. Commit with the code unit — not after every build. **No PR until freeze ends.** |
| QA | Handoff on disk. Usually no commit; fold test fixes into the cluster. **No PR until freeze ends.** |
| PM | Docs/canvas on disk. No PR just to mark Done; ride next code PR after freeze (or docs batch when asked). |

## Orchestrated multi-role runs

`прогони pipeline` / `сделай сам`: emit handoff files per role. Git: **one (or few) commits** for the finished **code** cluster. **Do not open a PR during the freeze** — at most one PR after 2026-09-01.

## Hook

`.cursor/hooks/git-policy-stop.sh` may nudge on a **very dirty** tree with **code** changes (commit reminder only during freeze). It must **not** ask to open a PR before 2026-09-01, and must **not** treat handoff-only dirt or archived gates as «open a PR now».
